Defaults for board features the macOS OS series calls into and pipa does not have yet.

First link of the pipa macOS 26.5 kernel (kernel-build.yml, 2026-11-11) stopped on undefined
native_owner_root_accepted and native_owner_root_mount_device (macos-owner-root-authenticated-open.patch, which
expects the owner-root audit globals of offline-owner-root-binding-audit.patch, built only with XNU_OWNER_ROOT_AUDIT
and a source storage driver) and native_exit_trace (macos-droidvm-k27-parity.patch, a board hook UniXNU-sheng's
package defines). Without owner-root audit no root is accepted, so authenticated opens keep EAUTH as in unmodified
XNU; the exit trace is a no-op. It is a plain (strong) definition: a weak one is bound through Mach-O weak
lookup, which the linker writes as a chained-fixup import, and XnuPrelink accepts a kernel with no import
(kernel-build.yml run 42991705340: "Chained fixup imports are not supported"). A board archive that provides
the real trace replaces this definition.

